  "decisions": [
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_49cb0a0ad683822392c92de08a829cbfd192a734b88e3805e11e3aa7e93bf11e",
      "turn_id": "01a21ed8-96cb-7ea2-afc4-05b6753ddb52",
      "rationale": "The numbering names both candidate label chains and gives per-position IMGT assignments. The historical Fab recipe leaves paired-chain validation open. The installed backbone reader can independently identify the deposited chain it covers and quantify its model-1 representation in one inexpensive pass. If it reports a deficit, its location relative to the six annotated loops is still needed. The result will determine whether this reader can contribute to a reusable measurement of the pair.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdh3zjegxybq5z",
        "gxa_01m8fdh409cnqk4c72",
        "gxa_01m8fdhy12tc27nmqf"
      ],
      "ops": [
        "open_branch",
        "add_node"
      ],
      "outcome": "adopted"
    },
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_2d7da5af0f2a0e125f898fe0be1d28f0b83b4f786c228a4a593a4a827986fd16",
      "turn_id": "01a21edb-3415-7602-b891-6eed1f654d1e",
      "rationale": "The IMGT map identifies both chains and fixes each CDR denominator independently of the coordinates. The single-chain method recorded an execution failure. The paired reader can check deposition and polymer identity and localize coverage in one local job. Its output should distinguish numbering gaps from unobserved assigned sites and establish which coordinate comparisons the archive supports.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdh409cnqk4c72",
        "gxa_01m8fdh3zjegxybq5z",
        "gxa_01m8fdptctj2h919s3",
        "gxa_01m8fdptfngart5992",
        "gxa_01m8fds04c6hxv10kv"
      ],
      "ops": [
        "open_branch",
        "add_node"
      ],
      "outcome": "adopted"
    },
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_cf8200f1d28c541206f7aeeda56d1ed28aa8cc49fdd62e3b10c558c3d647b58c",
      "turn_id": "01a21edd-1858-7390-943b-3bedb74e07b2",
      "rationale": "The supplied IMGT map assigns 8, 10 and 9 residues to VH CDR1–3 and 11, 3 and 9 to VL CDR1–3. The commissioned paired reader checks those assignments against the deposited polymers and coordinates. Its job has succeeded according to the catalogue, and the result is awaiting delivery. Reading its six loop masks and atom rule will resolve the curator’s question without a duplicate job and provide a tested node for the reusable workflow.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdh409cnqk4c72",
        "gxa_01m8fdh3zjegxybq5z",
        "gxa_01m8fdptctj2h919s3"
      ],
      "ops": [],
      "outcome": "maintained"
    },
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_d11c81720548c19e7fd3f56bcb14d8d30dfdcaea955371ff9a0bd55b594be2e2",
      "turn_id": "01a21edd-ef27-7b23-9db1-63661bfbae4d",
      "rationale": "The paired reader accepted the map for 4FAB assembly 1 and recovered the annotated heavy chain B (entity 2) and κ light chain A (entity 1). The map assigns 8, 10 and 9 positions to VH CDR1–3 and 11, 3 and 9 to VL CDR1–3. In fab_coverage.json each loop's matched count equals its assigned count, giving {{metric:matched_positions}} positive-occupancy model-1 Cα sites across {{metric:mapped_positions}} assignments. This supports Cα trace comparisons at shared IMGT positions. Repeating this measurement would add no evidence about the other backbone atoms. The tested workflow is available as paired-fab-imgt-ca-coverage@1.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdt6eg6y2eqwzc",
        "gxa_01m8fdh409cnqk4c72",
        "gxa_01m8fdh3zjegxybq5z"
      ],
      "ops": [
        "close_run"
      ],
      "outcome": "adopted"
    }
